  "seoBody": "<h2>How do you audit a care at home or housing support service in Scotland?</h2><p>Care at home and housing support are regulated by the Care Inspectorate in Scotland, not CQC, which applies in England only. Both are evaluated against the Health and Social Care Standards and the Care Inspectorate's quality framework, with key questions on care and support, staffing and leadership, graded on a six-point scale from unsatisfactory to excellent. Auditing your own service means self-evaluating against that framework honestly and continuously, and evidencing each judgement.</p><p>The difference from a care home is that the work is out in the community, across many homes and a dispersed patch. So the practical challenge is capturing honest, dated evidence at the point of a quality-assurance visit, not writing the self-evaluation from memory back at the office.</p><h2>Housing support self-evaluation</h2><p>Housing support self-evaluation is the process by which the service judges its own quality against the same Care Inspectorate quality framework and standards. An inspector looks at how well a service understands itself and whether its self-evaluation is honest and matched by action. A service that grades itself generously and cannot show the improvement work behind the grade fares worse than one that is candid about a weakness and can show what it is doing about it. Self-evaluation does not raise the grade; acting on it, through a live improvement plan, does.</p><h2>How quickler captures it</h2><p>Quickler turns a quality-assurance visit or a self-evaluation walk into a workflow that runs over the WhatsApp Business API. The manager or senior answers each prompt in their existing WhatsApp chat, with text, a voice note or a photo, tied to the quality indicator it evidences. Voice notes are transcribed automatically, so a senior on a doorstep can dictate an observation and move on. Every finding becomes an action in the improvement plan with an owner and a date, and a provider working several areas sees each service's position on a single dashboard.</p><p>Pricing is only for active users: £20 per active user a month, £20 minimum, dormant users free. An active user is someone who completed at least two workflows that month. The free tier is 20 reports a month and up to 10 photos per report, no card and no trial clock.</p><h2>What quickler is not</h2><p>Quickler is not a care management, rostering, scheduling or clinical system, and holds no personal care data. It captures the evaluation and evidence layer: observations against quality indicators, consented photos of a setting, the state of a personal plan at the point of a spot check. Personal plans, medication records and personal care logs stay in your care planning and rostering systems, which remain the single source of truth.</p><p>Quickler is not affiliated with or endorsed by the Care Inspectorate, and whether your evidence satisfies an inspection is a judgement for you and your inspector. This page is general information, not regulatory advice; always work from the current published framework and standards.</p><h2>Frequently asked questions</h2><h3>Can quality-assurance visits be done over WhatsApp?</h3><p>Yes. The manager or senior receives each prompt in their existing WhatsApp chat and replies with text, a voice note or a photo against each quality indicator, from any doorstep. No app or login, and no personal care data is entered.</p><h3>Does quickler replace our rostering or care management system?</h3><p>No. Quickler is the evaluation and evidence layer only. Rostering, scheduling, visit logging and medication records stay in your existing systems, which remain the single source of truth.</p><h3>How much does it cost?</h3><p>£20 per active user a month, £20 minimum, dormant users free, with a free tier of 20 reports a month and up to 10 photos per report.</p><h3>Related guides</h3><ul><li><a href=\"/pages/care-inspectorate-compliance-software-scotland.html\">Care Inspectorate compliance software</a></li><li><a href=\"/pages/care-inspectorate-self-evaluation-scotland.html\">Care Inspectorate self-evaluation</a></li><li><a href=\"/pages/care-inspectorate-mock-inspection-checklist-scotland.html\">Care Inspectorate mock inspection checklist</a></li></ul>",
